{"packet_id":"D067-03","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Anti-Eviction Act coverage and just-cause eviction","requirement":"The Anti-Eviction Act's just-cause eviction protections cover most residential rentals, and a landlord may end a tenancy only for the Act's statutory causes, after serving the required Notice to Quit.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Most residential rentals: single-family homes, mobile homes and mobile home park land, apartment buildings, complexes, and rooming and boarding homes.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes hotel, motel and seasonal or transient guests, and a unit held in trust for a permanently occupying developmentally disabled immediate family member."},"exemptions":"Two- or three-unit owner-occupied premises with two or fewer rental units; transient hotel, motel and guest-house guests; a unit held in trust for an immediate family member who is developmentally disabled and permanently occupies it.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1","quoted_span":"The Anti-Eviction Act applies to most residential rental properties including single-family homes, mobile homes and land in a mobile home park, apartment buildings, and complexes. This law also applies to rooming and boarding homes (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-53 to -84).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-03","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Ban on self-help evictions and lockouts","requirement":"A landlord may not evict a tenant by self-help—entering the unit, changing locks, shutting off utilities or blocking entry to force a move—without a court judgment; only a court officer may physically evict.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All residential tenants in New Jersey.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Landlord may be liable for damages, including court costs and reasonable attorney fees, and may be charged with disorderly conduct.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:39-1","quoted_span":"“Self-help” eviction is entry into a dwelling unit and removal of tenants without their consent or without a judgment from a court, are not permitted in New Jersey under any circumstances.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-03","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Relocation assistance for no-fault eviction","requirement":"A tenant evicted under the Act's no-fault causes cannot be removed until the landlord provides relocation assistance; for an illegal-occupancy eviction the payment equals six times the tenant's monthly rent.","key_value":"6 times monthly rent; 18% per year interest if unpaid","coverage_conditions":"Tenants evicted under N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1(g) or (h) causes, including health-and-safety abatement, illegal occupancy, and removal from the rental market.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Tenants evicted under the no-fault causes in N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1(g) or (h)."},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Landlord must repay municipal relocation funds advanced; unpaid relocation becomes a lien on the property and accrues 18% interest per year.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1","quoted_span":"Any tenant evicted under G 3) (illegal occupancy) is entitled to relocation assistance in an amount equal to six times the tenant’s monthly rent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-03","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"One-year stay of eviction for special circumstances","requirement":"A tenant facing eviction may ask the court for a stay of up to one year because of special circumstances, if all rent due is paid; the landlord and tenant may agree to extend it.","key_value":"up to 1 year","coverage_conditions":"Tenants in eviction proceedings who show special circumstances.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Tenants in eviction actions seeking a stay for special circumstances."},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-59.1","quoted_span":"If permission is granted, the tenant may not stay in the premises for more than one year, unless there is an agreed upon extension between landlord and tenant.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-03","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Rent increase must not be unconscionable and must comply with rent control","requirement":"A rent increase must not be unconscionable and must comply with all other applicable laws or municipal ordinances, including rent control; a tenant may withhold the unconscionable portion pending a court ruling.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Residential rent increases for tenants protected by the Anti-Eviction Act.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Rent increases challenged as unconscionable or governed by municipal rent control."},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1","quoted_span":"The rent increase must not be unconscionable and must comply with all other laws or municipal ordinances, including rent control.","interaction":"Increase must also comply with local rent control ordinances.","confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
